description:
Design a clock divider that generates a slower version of an input clock signal. The module takes an input clock (clk_in) and a reset signal, and it outputs a divided clock signal (clk_out). The division factor is specified by the parameter "divide_by". On each rising edge of clk_in, if reset is high, clk_out is set to low, and the counter is reset. Otherwise, the module increments a counter until it reaches the value of "divide_by - 1", at which point it toggles clk_out and resets the counter, effectively creating a clock output that runs at a frequency reduced by the specified division factor.
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  input reset,
  output reg clk_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  input reset,
  output reg clk_out
);parameter divide_by = 2;

reg [31:0] counter;

always @(posedge clk_in or posedge reset) begin
  if (reset) begin
    clk_out <= 1'b0;
    counter <= 0;
  end
  else begin
    if (counter == divide_by - 1) begin
      clk_out <= ~clk_out;
      counter <= 0;
    end
    else begin
      counter <= counter + 1;
    end
  end
end

endmodule

