description:
Design a circuit that generates a heartbeat signal by toggling an LED. The module takes a clock input and uses a 26-bit counter that increments on each clock cycle. The most significant bit of the counter is assigned to the LED output, effectively creating a slow pulsing effect. This design allows the LED to blink at a frequency determined by the clock, providing a visual indicator at a predefined interval.
module top_module(
	clk,
	led
);

code:
module top_module(
	clk,
	led
);parameter DUR_BITS = 26;

input  clk;
output led;





reg [(DUR_BITS-1):0] cnt;
always @ (posedge clk)
begin
	cnt <= cnt + 1;
end

assign led = cnt[DUR_BITS-1];



endmodule

