description:
Implement a 16-bit to 64-bit sign extension circuit. The module takes a 16-bit input, extracting the sign bit from the most significant bit (MSB) and replicating it across the higher 48 bits to ensure proper sign representation in the 64-bit output. The lower 16 bits of the output are directly taken from the input. This operation is crucial for correctly handling signed integers in a larger bit width.
module top_module(
  input [15:0] num_in,
  output reg [63:0] num_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [15:0] num_in,
  output reg [63:0] num_out
);reg [47:0] sign_bits; // 48 replicated sign bits

  // replicate sign bit
  always @(*) begin
    sign_bits = {48{num_in[15]}};
  end

  // concatenate sign bits with num_in
  always @(*) begin
    num_out = {sign_bits, num_in};
  end

endmodule

