description:
Design a circuit that implements a retiming block, which delays a set of input signals by a specified number of clock cycles. This module has a parameterized width \( n \) for the data signals and a delay \( d \), with a shift register being utilized to hold the input data across clock cycles. On each rising edge of the clock, the input data is shifted through the register, and the output reflects the value of the input after \( d \) clock cycles, thus performing synchronization and delay functions for digital signal processing applications or pipeline stages.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  input clk,
  output reg [n-1:0] out // Change output to 'reg' type
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  input clk,
  output reg [n-1:0] out // Change output to 'reg' type
);parameter n = 4; // number of data signals
parameter d = 2; // delay of the retiming block

reg [n-1:0] shift_reg [0:d-1]; // shift register for delaying input data signals

integer i;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  // shift data into the shift register
  for (i = d-1; i > 0; i = i - 1) begin
    shift_reg[i] <= shift_reg[i-1];
  end
  shift_reg[0] <= in;

  // synchronize output data signals with input clock signal
  out <= shift_reg[d-1]; // This is now valid since out is a reg
end

endmodule

