description:
Design a simple combinational logic circuit that processes a 2-bit input and generates a 2-bit output. The output's most significant bit (data_out[1]) is the result of an XOR operation between the two input bits (data_in[1] and data_in[0]), while the least significant bit (data_out[0]) directly mirrors the most significant input bit (data_in[1]). This configuration can be interpreted as a basic level of data manipulation, combining elements of logic gates to create derived output values based on the input states.
